<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p>If you are unsure about what to do with that bag of bulgur in your pantry, you&rsquo;re not alone. It&rsquo;s just not as popular as grains like brown rice or quinoa here in the U.S. But you&rsquo;re in the right place.&nbsp;</p>



<p>I grew up eating (and cooking) this ancient grain on the regular, and on this site, you&rsquo;ll find plenty of approachable and flavorful recipes using bulgur wheat. Start with this Turkish bulgur pilaf recipe, and when you are ready for more, learn <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/how-to-cook-bulgur/">How To Prepare and Cook Bulgur like rice</a> or try my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/one-pot-chicken-with-cardamom-bulgur/">Chicken with Bulgur</a> and <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/easy-tabbouleh-recipe/">Tabbouleh Salad</a> recipes.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Turkish-bulgur-pilaf-2.jpg" alt="Turkish bulgur pilaf in a pot with a wooden spoon on the side." class="wp-image-81485" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Turkish-bulgur-pilaf-2.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Turkish-bulgur-pilaf-2-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Turkish-bulgur-pilaf-2-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Turkish-bulgur-pilaf-2-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Turkish-bulgur-pilaf-2-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Turkish-bulgur-pilaf-2-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Turkish-bulgur-pilaf-2.jpg"></figure>


