<div id="recipe-13256-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-13256-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="13256"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-13256-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Saute onion and tomato paste: Heat olive oil in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Add in onion, cumin and green pepper and saute until translucent, 4-5 minutes.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Course-bulgur-pilaf-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person showing how to saute veggies to make bulgur wheat pilaf." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Course-bulgur-pilaf-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Course-bulgur-pilaf-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Course-bulgur-pilaf-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Course-bulgur-pilaf-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Course-bulgur-pilaf.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Course-bulgur-pilaf.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-13256-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Stir in the minced garlic and sautee for 30 seconds. Add in tomato paste and stir constantly for a minute or so.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-13256-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add in bulgur wheat, tomatoes, chickpeas, and water (or stock). Season it with salt and pepper.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-13256-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Stir to combine, bring it to a boil, put the lid on, and turn down the heat to low. Let it simmer for 10-12 minutes or until most of the liquid is absorbed.</span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bulgur-with-tomato-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Bulgur pilaf before and after it is cooked." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bulgur-with-tomato-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bulgur-with-tomato-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bulgur-with-tomato-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bulgur-with-tomato-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bulgur-with-tomato.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bulgur-with-tomato.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-13256-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Off the heat, allow it to rest for 10 minutes (with the lid on), fluff it with a fork, garnish with parsley, and serve.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>
